<li id="S3.I4.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S3.I4.i8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">23</span></span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Global Average Pooling;</p>
</div></li>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.20" class="ltx_listingline">
<li id="S3.I4.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S3.I4.i9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">24</span></span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Dense(128, ReLU), Dense(1, Sigmoid);</p>
</div></li>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.21" class="ltx_listingline">
<li id="S3.I4.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S3.I4.i10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">25</span></span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Initial learning rate: 0.001;</p>
</div></li>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.22" class="ltx_listingline">
<li id="S3.I4.i11" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S3.I4.i11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">26</span></span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Steps per epoch: <math id="S3.I4.i11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="num\_train\_samples/batch\_size" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">num\_train\_samples/batch\_size</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.23" class="ltx_listingline">
<li id="S3.I4.i12" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S3.I4.i12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">27</span></span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Exponential decay learning rate schedule;</p>
</div></li>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.24" class="ltx_listingline">
<li id="S3.I4.i13" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S3.I4.i13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">28</span></span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compile model (Adam, Binary Crossentropy, Accuracy);</p>
</div></li>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.25" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.25.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return:</span> Compiled CNN model;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.26" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Machine Unlearning Mechanism</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Machine unlearning refers to the concept where a model forgets or discards data used for training. This is particularly useful when certain data becomes irrelevant or when privacy issues arise (such as removing data associated with a specific individual).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the process of machine unlearning, the model is first trained on the entire dataset. For each sample, an influence score is computed based on the gradients of the model’s predictions with respect to the loss function. This score measures how much a particular sample contributed to the model’s learning. The influence score for sample <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Influence Score for sample i}=\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(f(\mathbf{x}_{i}),y_{i})\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Influence Score for sample i</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Influence Score for sample i}=\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(f(\mathbf{x}_{i}),y_{i})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is the gradient of the loss function <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the model’s prediction <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{x}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{x}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for sample <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the true label.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Based on these influence scores, certain samples (such as the least influential ones) are removed from the training dataset. The rationale is that removing these samples will not significantly degrade the model’s performance, but will help reduce the model’s reliance on less useful or sensitive data. Formally, we can identify and discard the samples with the smallest influence scores:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\text{remove}}=\{\mathbf{x}_{i}:\mathcal{I}(\mathbf{x}_{i})\text{ is among the lowest in }S\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>remove</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is among the lowest in </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\text{remove}}=\{\mathbf{x}_{i}:\mathcal{I}(\mathbf{x}_{i})\text{ is among the lowest in }S\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">After removing the data points with the lowest influence scores, the model is retrained on the reduced dataset. This mimics a ”forgetting” mechanism, as the model no longer has access to those removed data points, but retains the important features learned from the remaining data. Let <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\text{new}}=S\setminus S_{\text{remove}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>remove</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\text{new}}=S\setminus S_{\text{remove}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the new training set. The model is retrained using the reduced dataset:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}_{\text{new}}=\arg\min_{f}\sum_{\mathbf{x}_{i}\in S_{\text{new}}}\mathcal{L}(f(\mathbf{x}_{i}),y_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>new</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>f</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}_{\text{new}}=\arg\min_{f}\sum_{\mathbf{x}_{i}\in S_{\text{new}}}\mathcal{L}(f(\mathbf{x}_{i}),y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the model <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}_{\text{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>new</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}_{\text{new}}</annotation></semantics></math> is updated without the influence of the removed data points, effectively forgetting them while retaining the learned features from the remaining data. Figure <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3.1.1 Influence Score Calculation ‣ 3.1 Machine Unlearning Mechanism ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ MRD-LiNet: A Novel Lightweight Hybrid CNN with Gradient-Guided Unlearning for Improved Drought Stress Identification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> illustrates the overall machine unlearning framework, depicting key steps from influence score calculation to data removal and model retraining.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The influence score for each image in the dataset is calulated based on the gradients of the model’s predictions with respect to the input image, as explained below. The influence score indicates how much an individual image influences the model’s decision. The higher the influence score, the more sensitive the model’s prediction is to changes in that image.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.1.1 </span>Influence Score Calculation</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To quantify how much a sample contributes to learning, we define an influence score as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given a trained model <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> with parameters <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, the prediction for an input image <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}=f(\mathbf{x};\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}=f(\mathbf{x};\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">To quantify the effect of an image on the model’s decision, we compute an <span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">influence score</span> using gradients. The procedure consists of the following steps:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient Computation:</span>
For each image, compute the gradient of the prediction <math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the input <math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\hat{y}=\frac{\partial\hat{y}}{\partial\mathbf{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}\hat{y}=\frac{\partial\hat{y}}{\partial\mathbf{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I5.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This captures pixel-level sensitivity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Flattening:</span>
Each gradient tensor is flattened into a one-dimensional vector <math id="S3.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}</annotation></semantics></math> for ease of handling.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Concatenation:</span>
Gradients from all layers, <math id="S3.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{g}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{g}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, are concatenated into a single vector:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}=\text{Concat}(\mathbf{g}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{g}_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Concat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}=\text{Concat}(\mathbf{g}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{g}_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Norm Calculation:</span>
The L2 norm of <math id="S3.I5.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the influence score:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\|\mathbf{v}\|_{2}=\sqrt{\sum_{i}v_{i}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\|\mathbf{v}\|_{2}=\sqrt{\sum_{i}v_{i}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Final Result:</span>
Repeating the above steps for the dataset <math id="S3.I5.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> yields an array of scores:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}=[s_{1},s_{2},\dots,s_{N}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}=[s_{1},s_{2},\dots,s_{N}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.06367v1/machine_ul2.png" id="S3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:1489/796;" width="1489" height="796" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S3.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Machine Unlearning Framework</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>Calculate Influence Scores</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Trained model <math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, DataFrame <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> with image filenames and labels
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Array of influence scores <math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
              Initialize empty list <math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\leftarrow[~]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\leftarrow[~]</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm2.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.4.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">row <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
